<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oberkommando der Wehrmacht</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1938–1945</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as OKW, High Command of the Armed Forces</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Oberkommando der <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wehrmacht">Wehrmacht</a> (OKW), or High Command of the Armed Forces, was created by Hitler in February 1938 when he abolished the war ministry and took personal command of the German armed forces. Headed by Wilhelm Keitel, with Alfred Jodl as chief of operations, it served as Hitler's military staff and from 1942 directed every <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> except the Eastern Front.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oberkommando-der-wehrmacht.jpg" alt="Oberkommando der Wehrmacht" width="260" height="260" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_the_Oberkommando_der_Wehrmacht_W0224206.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
